Hmm, `filter` on text with background-clip:text — drop-shadow works with clipped text? drop-shadow on text with transparent fill: drop-shadow uses the alpha channel of the element's rendering, which includes the clipped gradient text → yes works and produces a glow following glyph shapes (standard technique).

Careful: `background-clip: text` + `filter` — the filter applies to the element after clipping; fine.

